    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nbasics\n\n### Description\n\nI currently use the following in my config:\r\n```vim\r\naugroup term\r\n    au TermOpen * setlocal listchars= nonumber norelativenumber\r\n    au TermOpen * startinsert\r\n    au BufEnter,BufWinEnter,WinEnter term://* startinsert\r\n    au BufLeave term://* stopinsert\r\naugroup END\r\n```\r\n\r\nBasics can already do startinsert, but doesn't seem to do it as extensively as this. The rest, it doesn't. I think this approximates what most nvim users do with their terminal, as the defaults (ie, do nothing special) are too rough around the edges.",
