        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nI tried initially to start Insert mode on every buffer enter, but it had several issues:\r\n- Some plugins open and close terminal inside their functionality, which lead to entering Insert mode in current non-terminal buffer. Don't quite remember which ones did this, but still.\r\n- I think it somewhat contradicts the overall Neovim workflow: after buffer switch I expect to always end up in Normal mode. It is different if I deliberately want to end up in terminal buffer, which `TermOpen` does. Besides, adding this will cause problems for traversing buffers when there are open terminal buffers.\r\n\r\nI'll think about local options, though. It does seem useful and universal enough.",
